From e687f2ae1a9760d67516284ab7e030928fdc505a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (draft)" <assistant@example.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 10:37:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: presence confirmation gates the humidity-delta cutoff
 (ADR-0003)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the old 'presence absent cuts immediately' policy with a
confirmation-gate model: water is cut only when max_humidity_delta is
exceeded AND presence has been detected within
presence_confirmation_window_seconds (default 60s). Delta alone no
longer cuts water; presence absence alone no longer cuts water.

Rationale: the actuator is a supply valve, not the showerhead itself —
presence going absent doesn't mean water is being wasted, and delta
alone risks false cuts from non-shower humidity sources. The
confirmation window tolerates brief mmWave presence-sensor dropouts
mid-shower instead of requiring continuous detection.

Also:
- Decouples max_session_seconds from presence_sensor's mere presence.
  Off by default unless explicitly configured, independent of presence.
- Adds presence support to replay.py (closes a previously-deferred
  BACKLOG item) — without it, replay could no longer exercise the
  primary cutoff path at all.
- Adds ADR-0003 documenting the full rationale and consequences.
- Rewrites all presence/delta tests across test_decision.py,
  test_init.py, test_actuator_integration.py, and test_replay.py to
  match the new semantics (97/97 passing).

Bumps version to 1.4.0.

BREAKING: deployments relying on delta-alone cuts with no
presence_sensor configured will need max_session_seconds as their
cutoff mechanism now, since delta can never confirm without presence
data.
